{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/666264-question-about-fae-titles-and-the-grimm-seeming-in-2ed","id":666264,"title":"Question About Fae Titles And The Grimm Seeming In 2ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-15T18:36:08-07:00","id":666264,"title":"Question About Fae Titles And The Grimm Seeming In 2ed","content":"To become a Grimm, do you necessarily have to assume the role of a character in a traditional and well known fairy tale, or can it be something more modern and not strictly tied to fairy tales? I would like to play changelings who consciously model themselves after the ideas of Alice from Alice In Wonderland and Sherlock Holmes, for example.<br /> <br /> How do the True Fae change their Titles between their manifestations of Realm, Actor, Prop and Wisp? They probably don't turn Realm into the other types because that is where they keep all their stuff and servants. But what if a True Fae decides to store a Title currently invested into a Realm as a Prop in her pocket to transform it into a Realm again somewhere else in the Hedge? Do all the buildings and other structures of the Realm suddenly transform into homogeneous thorns and brambles vaguely shaped like what they were before? I assume investing Titles into Realms outside the Hedge is impossible, though clever use of Contracts and Pledges might let parts of the Realm connect to the mortal world. Also, how often can the True Fae change their Titles from one type to another? I assume it has a limit, like once per scene or chapter. I didn't see any mention of costs like Willpower dots or anything like that. I can't find answers for all of this in Equinox Road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T18:46:34-07:00","id":666291,"title":"","content":"No commentary on the Grimm, since, you know, it's not out. Buuuut.<br /> <br /> First off, there's a distinction between Realms and Domains. All Strangers have a Domain-they have a set with pieces and actors, but the set is not important. The underground kingdom in Pan's Labyrinth that we never really see is a Domain, and if we stretch our imagination a little, the labyrinth and 'gate' are also Domains-interesting and pertinent to the plot, and yet not really wholly significant on it's own-hell, even the household is more important than the labyrinth. A Realm, on the other hand, is Important. It's Mount Doom, it's the Goblin King's Labyrinth, it's the Stone Table, it's the Amityville House. These are places where Things Happen, places that have their own character and story and set of Inevitabilites.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I would argue that a Title can't shift until it fulfills it's purpose in the Legend currently being played out, but by and large a True Fae by the rules as written can shift them whenever they need to. That sounds lame, so like I said, I would argue that a Title is locked into a Role until the Legend it's engaged in is played out, at which point it and the associated Domain shift to Arcadian whim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T19:37:36-07:00","id":666322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/666264-question-about-fae-titles-and-the-grimm-seeming-in-2ed#post666264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To become a Grimm, do you necessarily have to assume the role of a character in a traditional and well known fairy tale, or can it be something more modern and not strictly tied to fairy tales? I would like to play changelings who consciously model themselves after the ideas of Alice from Alice In Wonderland and Sherlock Holmes, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arc's right that we don't have specifics on Grimms. Though were I to speculate, I'd say more modern stuff would definitely be fair game.* Grays are a Kith, after all. One could make up explanations against, of course, but sight unseen, it would strike me as odd if similarly modern tales weren't kosher.<br /> <br /> * Obviously does not apply if you're playing in Dark Eras or something. &gt;.&gt; Hard to model oneself after Sherlock Holmes before the birth of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T19:58:26-07:00","id":666344,"title":"","content":"Yeah. This commentary is on target. Since it's literally an addition to the Grimm's Fairy Tales publication date Dark Era, the assumption is you're playing whatever's strong in the public zeitgeist. In the modern day, a Grimm Seeming may have followed the rules of horror films in order to escape, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T02:41:36-07:00","id":666649,"title":"","content":"So can I run the whole <b><i>The Wolf Among Us</i> </b>modern game with using Grimm Seeming as <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;fables&quot;? They all are Grimms, with Snow White from Princess Kith, Bigby Wolf from Wolfman Kith, etc.? </span></span></span><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Because game's backstory sounds just as the great example for the near-modern <b>Changeling</b> chronicle. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf Among Us Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Wolf Among Us</i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> is set in the year 1986, decades before the events of the first issue of </span></span></span><i>Fables</i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. For years, many of the magical and mystical lands described in myth, legend, and folklore (known colloquially as &quot;the homelands&quot;) have been occupied by an enigmatic tyrant known only as the Adversary. To escape the Adversary's marauding armies and totalitarian regime many creatures and characters known as &quot;fables&quot; fled to the </span></span></span>mundane world<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> and created an enclave known as Fabletown in colonial America, now located in modern-day Manhattan. To mask their presence from the native humans (referred to as &quot;mundies&quot;) all non-human fables have to purchase an enchantment known as a &quot;glamour&quot; which allows them to appear human, or be relocated to a rural community known as &quot;The Farm&quot;. The reformed </span></span></span>Big Bad Wolf<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, Bigby Wolf </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, is the sheriff of Fabletown and is responsible for hiding the community from the wider world and enforcing its laws.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-16-2015, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T04:22:56-07:00","id":666695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/666264-question-about-fae-titles-and-the-grimm-seeming-in-2ed?p=666649#post666649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can I run the whole <b><i>The Wolf Among Us</i> </b>modern game with using Grimm Seeming as <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;fables&quot;? They all are Grimms, with Snow White from Princess Kith, Bigby Wolf from Wolfman Kith, etc.? </span></span></span><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Because game's backstory sounds just as the great example for the near-modern <b>Changeling</b> chronicle. </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see any immediate reasons why it wouldn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T15:24:52-07:00","id":668875,"title":"","content":"Fingers crossed. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T22:05:23-07:00","id":670482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/666264-question-about-fae-titles-and-the-grimm-seeming-in-2ed?p=666344#post666344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. This commentary is on target. Since it's literally an addition to the Grimm's Fairy Tales publication date Dark Era, the assumption is you're playing whatever's strong in the public zeitgeist. In the modern day, a Grimm Seeming may have followed the rules of horror films in order to escape, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> When escaping, remember to double tap your Keeper!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T01:40:09-07:00","id":670611,"title":"","content":"Although now I wonder if Grimms can cause genre shifts, a technique suggested in &quot;How to survive in a horror movie.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;My life has become a horror movie of the splatterpunk genre? Veto! Time to make this a wuxia movie and make use of my brawl 5.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T20:20:54-07:00","id":671655,"title":"","content":"Now I want to play Atlanta Burns as a Grimm slasher-survivor of some variety, probably in an anger court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}